# opsx-prototype

Use this command as the entrypoint for the bundled `opsx-prototype` skill.

> Optional capability (default off). This skill is gated by the `prototype` feature flag and is only installed when explicitly enabled (e.g. `init --tool <tool> --feature prototype`). It uses external browser-automation / visual-analysis tools *if available*, otherwise it degrades gracefully to "user-pasted screenshot / verbal description". No API keys or platforms are built in.

## Intent

Turn a prototype link / screenshot / description into a structured requirement (screens / components / interactions / data / states) to feed `opsx-analysis`.

The canonical skill entry is:
- `{{skillsDir}}/opsx-prototype/SKILL.md`

## When to use it

Use `opsx-prototype` when you want to:
- convert a UI prototype into structured requirements before analysis
- extract screens, components, interactions, data fields, and states
- separate visible facts from inferences and open questions

## Recommended flow

1. Collect prototype input; detect external tools or degrade to user-provided material.
2. Extract screens / components / interactions / data / states, tagging certainty.
3. Produce a structured requirement and hand off to `opsx-analysis`.

## Relationship

- Downstream: output feeds `opsx-analysis`; open questions can go to `opsx-clarify`.
- Degrades to user-pasted screenshots / verbal description when external tools are unavailable.

## Default output mode

By default, produce the structured requirement in the conversation.

## Suggested first action

Open or invoke the bundled skill and continue from:

- `{{skillsDir}}/opsx-prototype/SKILL.md`
